    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0164" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1401</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d150-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-29T21:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918,
                                9 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 30, 7.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Moscow press prints to-day: “American Consul informed Supreme Economic Council
                    that American Government agrees to resume commercial and industrial relations
                    with Russia, regardless of repudiation of debts.” Suppose Department authorized
                    such statement, if made. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
